    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="f2fd4129-33ee-5c74-ba0a-8e4210d8a60b" activityNameId="a325c258-a036-5a84-9031-4bf9155cd0c9" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Biogas, from fodder beet, co-digestion, at storage</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Biogas, from fodder beet, co-digestion, at storage
The data set describes the anaerobic digestion of fodder beets in co-digestion. The fodder beets have a dry matter content of 0.15. A minimum of 11 % of the produced biogas needs to be burned in a cogeneration unit in order to meet the full heat demand and part of the electricity demand of the digestion unit.;
UUID: 1db69a18-bc2a-3a8a-aa77-63e515022d6b
This data set includes the production of the substrate, transports of the substrates, the biogas plant infrastructure, the consumption of heat and electricity, the application of the digestates, and direct emissions to air.
Location: Data valid for Switzerland
Technology: Anaerobic digestion at mesophilic temperature.
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: Questionnaire and literature study 
Extrapolations: &lt;null&gt;
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_1db69a18-bc2a-3a8a-aa77-63e515022d6b.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
